# flipbook.fmat — the sprite-sheet grid, as a material.
#
# This was `sheet_cols:`/`sheet_rows:` on every sprite and every particle layer,
# which is odd when you look at it: how a texture divides up is a property of
# the ART, and the same four-by-four sheet had to be described again on every
# sprite that wore it.
#
# What stays on the object is the FRAME. Which cell this particular sprite is
# showing is not a property of the art, and a script animating one sprite has no
# business moving every other sprite wearing the same material.
kind: sprite
texture: square
doc: A 4x4 sheet. The object picks the cell with its own frame number.
effects:
  - effect: sprite_sheet
    cols: 4
    rows: 4
  - effect: blend_mode
    mode: alpha
